=== Prompt for SKY-006-a (attempt 1) ===
Implement user story SKY-006-a: Code review document generation: Skyscanner mini-app

## Story Description
The review agent performs live inspection of all src/ files in /tmp/skyscanner-app and produces the structured review document at /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/SKY-006-review.md. This story covers document creation and content correctness only; automated gate execution is covered by SKY-006-b.

## Acceptance Criteria
- PREREQUISITE — /tmp/skyscanner-app/src exists and is non-empty before the agent begins; if absent or empty the agent halts immediately with a dependency error message referencing the missing path and does not create the review directory or file
- The review directory /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/ is created by the agent if it does not already exist before writing the output file
- The file /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/SKY-006-review.md is created (or overwritten) containing exactly six H2 sections appearing in this order: ## TypeScript, ## Tests, ## Security, ## Error Handling, ## Express Safety, ## Verdict
- No H2 section other than the six listed above appears in the document, and no section is duplicated
- Each of the five category sections (TypeScript, Tests, Security, Error Handling, Express Safety) must contain either: (a) at least one finding entry that includes a concrete file path relative to /tmp/skyscanner-app/src and, where applicable, a line-number reference derived from live inspection of the actual source files, OR (b) an explicit statement such as 'No issues found' — sections must never be empty or omitted, and static placeholder text not referencing a real inspected file is prohibited
- The agent must perform a fresh live inspection of /tmp/skyscanner-app/src on every invocation; it is explicitly prohibited from reading, reusing, or re-emitting any previously generated or cached version of /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/SKY-006-review.md as its output
- The ## Verdict section contains exactly one line matching the regex `^Verdict: (PASS|FAIL)$` as its first non-blank content line — this format uses a colon-prefix to maintain consistency with sibling document SKY-006-b
- When the verdict is FAIL, the ## Verdict section includes a prioritised numbered list of blocking findings immediately following the 'Verdict: FAIL' line, with each item referencing the originating category section
- When the verdict is PASS, the ## Verdict section contains no blocking-findings list (a brief summary sentence is permitted)
- The verdict is FAIL if and only if at least one finding across the five category sections is classified as blocking; the agent must apply consistent severity classification criteria across all categories
- The output file is UTF-8 encoded with Unix line endings (LF only, no CRLF)
- The document is syntactically valid Markdown: all headings use ATX style (`##`), list items are consistently formatted, and any code samples are enclosed in fenced code blocks with a language identifier

